            There are many consequences of having identity types between types in the dependent type theory. One such example is that any time one uses an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            in a definition, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Tarski+universes"} weak Tarski universes
            or typal large recursion principles for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+types"} inductive types
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/univalence"} univalence
            to the dependent type theory itself, which makes the identity types between types and equivalence types coincide with each other.
          %h2#definition_from_an_interval_type Definition from an interval type
          %p
            Suppose that one has an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+type"} interval type
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{I}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝕀
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0:\mathbb{I}
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %mi 𝕀
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1:\mathbb{I}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} ctx
                    %mrow
                      %mi Γ
                      %mo ⊢
                      %mi 𝕀
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} type
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac{\Gamma \; \mathrm{ctx}}{\Gamma \vdash \mathbb{I} \; \mathrm{type}}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
