          %h3#types_as_groupoids
            Types as
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            The suggestion that identity types witness
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            and
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
          %ul
            %li#HofmannStreicher98
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martin+Hofmann"}> Martin Hofmann
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Streicher"} Thomas Streicher
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The groupoid interpretation of type theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Giovanni+Sambin"} Giovanni Sambin
                et al. (eds.),
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Twenty-five years of constructive type theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://global.oup.com/academic/product/twenty-five-years-of-constructive-type-theory-9780198501275"} ISBN:9780198501275
                %a{:href => "http://www.mathematik.tu-darmstadt.de/~streicher/venedig.ps.gz"} ps
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/HofmannStreicherGroupoidInterpretation.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#AwodeyWarren07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Awodey"}> Steve Awodey
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Warren"} Michael Warren
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Homotopy theoretic models of identity type
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0709.0248"} arXiv:0709.0248
          %p
            This is ultimately verified by the observation that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J-rule"} J-rule
            makes the identity types interpret as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/very+good+path+space+objects"} very good path space objects
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+cartesian+closed+model+category"} locally cartesian closed model category
            (such as the
            = succeed "):" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
          %ul
            %li#Shulman12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mike+Shulman"}> Mike Shulman
              ,
              %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/03models.pdf#page=34"} Part III, around slide 34
              of:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Minicourse on homotopy type theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://home.sandiego.edu/~shulman/hottminicourse2012/"} web
          %p reviewed in:
          %ul
            %li#Riehl22
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"}> Emily Riehl
              , §1.1 in:
              = succeed "," do
